Supporting patch: hmac drops the libcrux-kats dev-dependency
Change: crates/algorithms/hmac/Cargo.toml: remove the dev-dependency on libcrux-kats (test vectors).
Why: libcrux-kats is not in the trimmed input set, and cargo must be able to load its manifest even for a build that does not compile tests.
Behaviour: no effect on the normal build or on any Rust source; only the test-only dependency edge is removed.
Classification: A-mechanical
Assumptions: none.
Obligations: none.
Independent: yes

diff --git a/crates/algorithms/hmac/Cargo.toml b/crates/algorithms/hmac/Cargo.toml
index b2e01835a..b1df3d714 100644
--- a/crates/algorithms/hmac/Cargo.toml
+++ b/crates/algorithms/hmac/Cargo.toml
@@ -23,4 +23,3 @@ libcrux-traits.workspace = true
 libcrux-macros = { version = "=0.0.3", path = "../../utils/macros" }
 
 [dev-dependencies]
-libcrux-kats = { path = "../../testing/kats", features = ["hmac"] }
